# Binaries
/hackerfive
*.exe
*.dll
*.so

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Go
vendor/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Test outputs
coverage.out
*.test

# Synced upstream templates (scripts/sync-nuclei-templates.sh) — never redistributed, see docs/10-implementation-plan-ph1b.md Step 2
.nuclei-templates-cache/

# Generated template metadata index (`hackerfive templates index`, docs/14-implementation-plan-ph5.md Step 3's R9) —
# regenerate on demand, would go stale the moment templates/ or the synced corpus changes if committed
/templates/index.json

# goreleaser output (goreleaser release --snapshot --clean)
dist/
# .claude/

# Local, per-engagement workspace: HackerOne/program credentials, pulled
# scope files, scan output, results logs — never committed. See
# .engagements/README.md.
.engagements/
.playwright-mcp/

# Credentials/config loaded by cmd/hackerfive/dotenv.go (HACKERFIVE_AUTH_TOKEN,
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY, etc.) — see .env.example for the real var names, never
# commit actual values.
.env

# I4-drafted templates (pkg/mcpserver's plan tool, Phase 6 Step 2) — local,
# untrusted, ephemeral until a human reviews and promotes one; never
# committed. Keep the directory itself tracked via .gitkeep.
/templates-proposed/*
!/templates-proposed/.gitkeep